# SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
#
# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the ASan lane (tools/ci_profile.py).
#
# Exactly one class of report is suppressed here (D-142): protobuf's generated
# file registration. When bessd dlopen()s a plugin, the plugin's generated
# protobuf code calls google::protobuf::internal::AssignDescriptors, which
# allocates the file's descriptor table once per process and never frees it --
# protobuf's descriptor structures are process-lifetime by design. `unload
# plugin` closes the library (so a rebuilt plugin is picked up), which is what
# makes those allocations unreachable at exit and therefore visible to LSan:
#
#   Direct leak of 96 byte(s) in 1 object(s) allocated from:
#       #0 operator new(unsigned long)
#       ...
#       #5 google::protobuf::internal::AssignDescriptors(...)
#       #6 <unknown module>          <- the closed plugin library
#
# Nothing else is suppressed: a bare `leak:*` would hide real leaks in the
# daemon, and this entry names the one protobuf entry point and nothing more.
leak:google::protobuf::internal::AssignDescriptors
